  "prefLabel": "Hum 313.02 Decisions on Motions for Waiver of Rules",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Hum 313.02 Decisions on Motions for Waiver of Rules. The presiding officer shall waive the rule if the waiver:\n\n(a) Appears to be lawful; and\n\n(b) Is more likely to promote a fair and accurate hearing than would adherence to the particular requirement or limitation set by the rule.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Hum 300) #8815-A, eff 2-3-07",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/hum100-300.html"
